To make the script more efficient for handling very large text files, you can consider the following optimizations:

1. Read the files line by line instead of loading the entire content into memory at once. This will reduce the memory usage and improve the script's performance for very large files. Here's how to modify the code:

```matlab
function uniqueWords = findUniqueWords(textFile1, textFile2)
    uniqueWords = [];

    fh1 = fopen(textFile1, 'rt');
    fh2 = fopen(textFile2, 'rt');
    %Initialize empty sets to store unique words
    wordSet1 = set([]);
    wordSet2 = set([]);
    while ~feof(fh1) && ~feof(fh2)
        %Read lines from both files
        line1 = fgetl(fh1);
        line2 = fgetl(fh2);

        %Split each line into words and add them to their respective sets
        words1 = strsplit(lower(line1), ' ');
        words2 = strsplit(lower(line2), ' ');
        for w1 = words1
            insert(wordSet1, w1);
        end
        for w2 = words2
            insert(wordSet2, w2);
        end
    end
    %Find unique words in wordSet1 that are not in wordSet2
    uniqueWords = setdiff(wordSet1, wordSet2);

    fclose(fh1);
    fclose(fh2);
end
```

