To implement the bubble sort algorithm in C++ with the given constraints, we'll create a function called `bubbleSort` that takes an array of integers and its size as parameters. Here's the implementation:

```cpp
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    bool swapped = true; // flag to check if any swap is needed in each iteration
    for (int i = 0; I < n - 1 && swapped; ++i) {
        swapped = false; // assume no swap will occur in this iteration
        for (int j = 0; j < n - I - 1; ++j) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) { // swap if current element is greater than next
                int temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                arr[j + 1] = temp;
                swapped = true; // update swapped flag if swap occurred
            }
        }
    }
}
```

